        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add poll unvote and option updates",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add bridge actions for native poll unvote and add-option updates\n- expose `imsg poll unvote` and `imsg poll add-option`\n- expose JSON-RPC `polls.unvote` / `polls.addOption` plus existing-style aliases\n- fix outgoing Polls creation payloads to keep `item.title` empty, matching native Messages payloads so options render as real poll choices\n- add status selector reporting, docs, changelog, and command/RPC coverage\n\n## Redacted proof\nProof collected on lobster with branch-local artifacts from `feat/poll-unvote-add-option` and freshly relaunched injected Messages.app sessions. Raw logs are kept local because they include chat GUIDs, message GUIDs, handles, and participant identifiers.\n\n- `main` head: `c541bea2828f773e85588d0598ed3565140736f2`\n- branch head with rendering fix: `3af173b`\n- before on `main`: `make build` passed; `imsg poll` help listed only `send|vote`; completions search for `poll unvote`, `poll add-option`, `polls.unvote`, and `polls.addOption` returned no matches\n- initial branch proof before the rendering fix: Messages recognized the payload as a Poll extension (`sent a poll` plus `Add Choice`) but the options did not visibly render as normal poll choices\n- payload diagnosis: received native Polls creation rows keep `item.title` empty and put the question in the separate caption row; our generated payload had duplicated the question into `item.title`, which made Messages collapse the option UI\n- after rendering fix: rebuilt branch-local `bin/imsg-bridge-helper.dylib`, relaunched Messages with `imsg launch --dylib \"$PWD/bin/imsg-bridge-helper.dylib\"`, and sent a new proof poll\n- fixed payload proof: archived outgoing payload has `item.title == \"\"`, `src=p&c=2`, and options `[Red, Blue]`\n- fixed visual proof: user observed the Messages UI render `Red` and `Blue` as poll options, not an empty options shell\n- after command/RPC surface: completions include `imsg poll unvote` and `imsg poll add-option`; status reports `poll.unvote`, `polls.unvote`, `messages.poll.unvote`, `poll.addOption`, `polls.addOption`, and `messages.poll.addOption`\n- live mutation proof in the redacted test group: sent the fixed poll with options `[Red, Blue]`, voted `Red` with `removed=false`, unvoted `Red` with `removed=true`, then added option `Green`\n- history readback: created poll decoded with the proof question and `[Red, Blue]`; unvote update decoded as `kind=vote`, `event=imessage.poll.voted`, `option_text=Red`, `event_type=removed`; add-option update decoded with option `[Green]`\n\n## Verification\n- `make build` ✅ after the rendering fix\n- GitHub CI ✅ for `3af173b` (`macos`, `linux-read-core`, Socket checks all pass)\n- `make test` ⚠️ blocked before project tests run on this host: `Tests/IMsgCoreTests/BridgeHelperLocatorTests.swift:2:8: error: no such module 'Testing'`\n- `make lint` ⚠️ blocked locally on lobster by SwiftLint/SourceKit: `Loading sourcekitdInProc.framework/Versions/A/sourcekitdInProc failed`\n",
